What was copied or adapted, and how it was changed:

- 2048_decision_ft/playjev_prompt.py
  From playjev/model.py, the plain-template builders only (openjev-letters-v1
  sentence, state block, lettered options, "Answer:" cue). The chat
  template, temporal frame stacking, and PlayJevModel runtime are not
  copied. The 2048 option sentences are the long descriptions from
  games/2048/pj_hook.js.

- 2048_decision_ft/prompt.py
  Same system sentence and plain "Answer:" layout. Modified so <state> is
  a text board, with short option phrases written here.

- 2048_decision_ft/vendor/pj_shim.js
  games/_shared/pj_shim.js. The script body is unchanged. An attribution
  header was added.

- 2048_decision_ft/vendor/pj_2048_hook.js
  games/2048/pj_hook.js. Modified by adding setGrid(rows), which paints a
  board that came from the Python engine and then calls the unchanged
  canvas()/frame() path.

- 2048_decision_ft/frame.py
  New PIL renderer. The 500x500 board geometry and the 448px JPEG quality
  0.85 contract follow pj_hook.js canvas() and pj_shim.js frame().

- 2048_decision_ft/board.py
  playjev/teachers/2048.py, simplified. The 64-bit nibble layout and the
  line heuristic match the teacher. Up and down go through a transpose
  instead of the column-unpack tables, and each move also returns the
  score gained. The teacher class is not copied.

- 2048_decision_ft/expert.py
  Not a copy of the teacher. The depth-2 expectimax, spawn odds, and
  temperature softmax follow playjev/teachers/2048.py. The search is
  rewritten and calls board.py.

- 2048_decision_ft/image_policy.py
  Not a copy of PlayJevModel. The letter-slot readout uses the same place
  in the network (last token of model.model) as PlayJevModel._forward.

- docs/site.css
  demo/demo.css, modified. PlayJev's rules are kept. Rules added for this
  front page are marked "PlayVLA additions" at the bottom of the file.

- docs/pj_silence.js
  demo/pj_silence.js. The script body is unchanged. An attribution header
  was added.

- docs/site.js
  Written here. It is not a copy of demo/demo.js. The theme toggle and
  sticky bar follow that demo.

- docs/games/<game>/
  The ten browser games, taken from PlayJev's demo/games/ bundle, which
  itself vendored other authors' games. Each game keeps that author's
  LICENSE and UPSTREAM. PlayJev's own patches inside those copies (the
  silence script, Pacman's read-only getters, Sokoban's Microban levels,
  and the notes in each CHANGES.md) are Apache-2.0. This repository
  removed PlayJev's training hooks so the pages play from the keyboard,
  and added the small front-page handles named in each CHANGES.md.

The image-training loss (cross-entropy between an expert soft target and
the model's letter distribution) is the same kind of objective as PlayJev
train_sft.py. That training script was not copied.

The text "Laya" in this repository names the convaiinnovations/laya model
used in experiments. It is not the PlayVLA site name, and those modules
were not renamed.
